{"seed":{"mim":"618229","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"MITOCHONDRIAL COMPLEX I DEFICIENCY, NUCLEAR TYPE 7","alt_titles":[],"symbol":"MC1DN7","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2015},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"MITOCHONDRIAL COMPLEX I DEFICIENCY, NUCLEAR TYPE 7","mim":"618229","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:26008862","type":"Paper","label":"Cameron et al. (2015)","pmid":"26008862","year":2015,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Exome sequencing identifies complex I NDUFV2 mutations as a novel cause of Leigh syndrome."},{"id":"paper:19167255","type":"Paper","label":"Pagniez-Mammeri et al. (2009)","pmid":"19167255","year":2009,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"supporting","title":"Rapid screening for nuclear genes mutations in isolated respiratory chain complex I defects."},{"id":"paper:12754703","type":"Paper","label":"Bénit et al. (2003)","pmid":"12754703","year":2003,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutant NDUFV2 subunit of mitochondrial complex I causes early onset hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and encephalopathy."},{"id":"paper:11220739","type":"Paper","label":"Loeffen et al. (2001)","pmid":"11220739","year":2001,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Mutations in the complex I NDUFS2 gene of patients with cardiomyopathy and encephalomyopathy."},{"id":"finding:11220739:1","type":"Finding","label":"In patients from 3 families with enzymatic complex I deficiency, cardiomyopathy and encephalomyopathy, Loeffen et al. (2001) screened NDUFS2 cDNA by RT-PCR and direct sequencing. They found 3 missense mutations that changed conserved amino acids.","pmid":"11220739","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS2","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS2"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001638","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cardiomyopathy","hpo_id":"HP:0001638"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001298","type":"Phenotype","label":"Encephalopathy","hpo_id":"HP:0001298"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0011923","type":"Phenotype","label":"Decreased activity of mitochondrial complex I","hpo_id":"HP:0011923"},{"id":"inh:AR","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal recessive","hpo_id":"HP:0000007"},{"id":"finding:11220739:2","type":"Finding","label":"Loeffen et al. (2001) noted a high rate of consanguinity and an autosomal recessive mode of inheritance in their group of patients with complex I deficiency. Together with the absence of common mtDNA mutations, this made a nuclear genetic cause likely.","pmid":"11220739","section":"inheritance"},{"id":"finding:12754703:1","type":"Finding","label":"Bénit et al. (2003) described 3 affected sibs from a consanguineous family who had complex I deficiency with early-onset hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and trunk hypotonia. The authors noted that this cardiomyopathy contrasted with the mainly neurologic symptoms seen with mutations in most other complex I subunit genes.","pmid":"12754703","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:NDUFV2","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFV2"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001639","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy","hpo_id":"HP:0001639"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008936","type":"Phenotype","label":"Axial hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0008936"},{"id":"finding:12754703:2","type":"Finding","label":"In 3 affected sibs from a consanguineous family with complex I deficiency and early-onset hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, Bénit et al. (2003) used denaturing HPLC and sequencing to identify a homozygous 4-bp deletion in intron 2 of the NDUFV2 gene (IVS2+5_+8delGTAA). The deletion altered the consensus splice-donor site of exon 2 and led to a 70% decrease in NDUFV2 protein and complex I deficiency.","pmid":"12754703","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:NDUFV2:raw:ivs2+5_+8delgtaa","type":"Variant","label":"NDUFV2 IVS2+5_+8delGTAA","gene":"NDUFV2","keys":["raw:ivs2+5_+8delgtaa"],"omim_name":"NDUFV2"},{"id":"finding:19167255:1","type":"Finding","label":"Pagniez-Mammeri et al. (2009) screened 8 patients with biochemically proven isolated mitochondrial complex I deficiency for mutations in 8 nuclear complex I genes (NDUFS1, NDUFS2, NDUFS3, NDUFS4, NDUFS7, NDUFS8, NDUFV1, and NDUFV2). They used Surveyor nuclease digestion of 22 cDNA fragments covering the coding sequences. Single-nucleotide polymorphisms and missense mutations were detected in 18.7% of the cDNA fragments, and molecular defects were identified in 3 patients.","pmid":"19167255","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS1","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS1"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS3","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS3"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS4","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS4"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS7","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS7"},{"id":"gene:NDUFS8","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFS8"},{"id":"gene:NDUFV1","type":"Gene","label":"NDUFV1"},{"id":"finding:19167255:2","type":"Finding","label":"Pagniez-Mammeri et al. (2009) concluded that Surveyor nuclease screening of cDNAs is a reliable and easy-to-interpret way to genotype nuclear complex I deficiencies, and that it reduces the number of sequencing reactions needed. They suggested that the method would make prenatal diagnosis more feasible.","pmid":"19167255","section":"diagnosis"},{"id":"finding:26008862:1","type":"Finding","label":"Cameron et al. (2015) reported 2 sibs with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and brain atrophy who were diagnosed with mitochondrial complex I deficiency based on low enzyme activity in muscle and a high lactate/pyruvate ratio in fibroblasts.","pmid":"26008862","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002059","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cerebral atrophy","hpo_id":"HP:0002059"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0032653","type":"Phenotype","label":"Elevated lactate:pyruvate ratio","hpo_id":"HP:0032653"},{"id":"finding:26008862:2","type":"Finding","label":"In 2 sibs with complex I deficiency, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, and brain atrophy, Cameron et al. (2015) identified compound heterozygous mutations in the NDUFV2 gene, found by whole-exome sequencing of fibroblast DNA from one sib and filtering for novel nonsynonymous changes: a previously reported intronic splice mutation (c.IVS2+1delGTAA), considered disease causing, and a novel 1-bp insertion (c.669_670insG) predicted to cause a frameshift (p.Ser224Valfs*3).","pmid":"26008862","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:NDUFV2:c.1delgtaa","type":"Variant","label":"NDUFV2 c.1delgtaa","gene":"NDUFV2","keys":["c.1delgtaa"],"omim_name":"NDUFV2, 1DELGTAA"},{"id":"variant:NDUFV2:c.669_670insg","type":"Variant","label":"NDUFV2 c.669_670insg / p.S224V","gene":"NDUFV2","keys":["c.669_670insg","p.S224V"],"omim_name":"NDUFV2, SER224VAL"},{"id":"finding:26008862:3","type":"Finding","label":"Cameron et al. (2015) reported a consanguineous family in which 3 of 5 sibs with complex I deficiency presented with Leigh syndrome but without cardiac involvement.","pmid":"26008862","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"phenotext:leigh syndrome","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"Leigh syndrome"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001626","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the cardiovascular system","hpo_id":"HP:0001626"},{"id":"finding:26008862:4","type":"Finding","label":"By screening of 10 probands with complex I deficiency from different families, Cameron et al. (2015) identified homozygosity for the NDUFV2 intronic c.IVS2+1delGTAA mutation in a consanguineous family with Leigh syndrome.","pmid":"26008862","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"finding:26008862:5","type":"Finding","label":"Cameron et al. (2015) noted that homozygosity for the c.IVS2+1delGTAA NDUFV2 mutation had previously been reported in 2 families presenting with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, truncal hypotonia, and encephalopathy, whereas their family with the same genotype had Leigh syndrome without cardiac involvement, expanding the clinical phenotype associated with this mutation.","pmid":"26008862","section":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:11220739","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:11220739:1"},{"src":"finding:11220739:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:molecular_genetics"},{"src":"finding:11220739:1","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:NDUFS2","pmid":"11220739"},{"src":"finding:11220739:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001638","pmid":"11220739","present":true,"text":"cardiomyopathy"},{"src":"finding:11220739:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001298","pmid":"11220739","present":true,"text":"encephalomyopathy"},{"src":"finding:11220739:1","rel":"has_pheno